292 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (On 9 October 2026, our school observed World Mental Health Day, which falls on 10 October, by organising a series of engaging competitions for students from Grades 1 to 10. The initiative, conducted by Jidnyasa Counselling & Guidance, aimed to raise awareness about mental health, encourage emotional expression, and emphasise the importance of mental well-being among students.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
293 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The competitions were thoughtfully designed to suit different age groups, providing students with meaningful opportunities to explore and express their understanding of mental health. Students from Grades 1 to 5 participated in a poster-making competition, conveying powerful messages through colourful illustrations and creative artwork. Students from Grades 6 to 8 showcased their thoughts and perspectives through an essay-writing competition, reflecting on emotional awareness, mental well-being, and the importance of nurturing a healthy mind. Meanwhile, students from Grades 9 and 10 participated in a mental health quiz that tested their knowledge of stress management, emotional well-being, self-care, and the importance of seeking help when needed.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
294 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The competitions witnessed enthusiastic participation and encouraged students to reflect on the significance of mental health in their everyday lives. The winners were felicitated with prizes in recognition of their creativity, knowledge, and sincere efforts.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Through this initiative, the school reinforced the message that mental health is just as important as physical health. Students were encouraged to acknowledge their emotions, practise self-care, seek support when necessary, and extend empathy and understanding towards others.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
296 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The observance served as a meaningful step towards fostering a supportive, compassionate, and emotionally healthy school community, where every student feels heard, valued, and encouraged to flourish.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
