/P 145 0 R
/E (The seminar explored the key components of physical education, including physical fitness, sports and games, health education, yoga and recreational activities. It highlighted how regular physical activity improves concentration, memory, confidence and emotional well-being while fostering teamwork, leadership, cooperation and sportsmanship.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
615 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The speakers also emphasised the importance of integrating physical education into the core curriculum, stressing that a healthy body supports a healthy mind. Teachers were encouraged to recognise sports and physical activities as essential learning experiences that instil perseverance, responsibility and lifelong healthy habits.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
616 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The session concluded with an energising warm-up exercise for the teachers, bringing the message of fitness to life through active participation. It served as a reminder that physical education is not merely a recreational pursuit but an integral part of meaningful education, preparing students to lead healthier, happier and more balanced lives.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
617 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 145 0 R
/E (The seminar inspired educators to champion an active lifestyle and create opportunities for students to discover their strengths through movement and play. It reaffirmed the belief that true education develops the mind, strengthens the body and builds character.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [8]
>>
