/E (The seminar on Teaching Students with Diverse Learning Needs, presented by Ms. Sangeeta Zanzale, explored inclusive teaching practices such as Universal Design for Learning \(UDL\), differentiated instruction, assistive technology and flexible assessment. Teachers were encouraged to recognise individual strengths and remove learning barriers to ensure meaningful learning opportunities for every child.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Mrs. Suvarna Panpatil highlighted the Importance of the Mother Tongue in Early Education in Multilingual Classrooms. The session explained how learning through a familiar language strengthens comprehension, confidence, cognitive development and early literacy. It encouraged teachers to respect linguistic diversity and connect the mother tongue with the language of instruction.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (Together, these sessions reinforced the belief that every child deserves to be heard, respected and supported. They inspired educators to embrace individual differences and nurture classrooms where diversity is valued and every learner has the opportunity to flourish.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
